hadiths[165]{hadithnumber,text}:
"496","Ali bin Hajar informed us, saying: Ali bin Mushar informed us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Suhail bin Abi Salih, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, He said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Whoever prays after Friday prayers, let him pray four.”"
"497","Ishaq bin Ibrahim told us, he said: Abba Sufyan, on the authority of Amr bin Dinar, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Salem, on the authority of his father, that the Messenger of God May God’s prayers and peace be upon him, he used to pray two rak’ahs after Friday prayers."
"498","Qutaibah bin Saeed told us, he said: Al-Layth told us, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, that it was, “When he prayed Friday, he would go away and pray I prostrated two times in his house, then he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to do that.”"
"499","Qutaibah bin Saeed told us, he said: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Abdullah bin Abi Bakr, on the authority of Abbad bin Tamim, on the authority of his uncle, that The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, “dragged water, prayed two rak’ahs, and turned his cloak around.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"500","Amr bin Ali told us, he said: Yazid told us, meaning bin Zuray’, he said: Yunus told us, on the authority of Al-Hasan, on the authority of Abu Bakra, he said: “We were With the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and the sun eclipsed, so he got up to the mosque dragging his robe from the wheel, so the people got up to him and he prayed two rak’ahs. as you pray\ (Peace Be Upon Him)"""""
"501","Ishaq bin Ibrahim told us, he said: Al-Walid bin Muslim reported, on the authority of Al-Awza’i, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Urwa, on the authority of Aisha, who said: “The sun was eclipsed during the time of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and a comprehensive prayer was called, and the people gathered, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, led them in prayer.” He said the salaam four rak'ahs, two rak'ahs, and four prostrations.\"" 502"""""
"502","'Abda ibn 'Abd al-Rahim informed us, saying: Ibn 'Uyaynah informed us, from Yahya ibn Sa'id, from 'Amrah, from 'A'ishah, that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ prayed during an eclipse in the manner of Zamzam (i.e., a specific description) — four rak'ahs in four prostrations. 'Ubayd ibn 'Umayr differed from them (in this narration)."
"503","Ishaq bin Ibrahim told us, he said: Abba Muadh bin Hisham, he said: My father told me, on the authority of Qatada, regarding the verses of prayer, on the authority of Ata, on the authority of Ubaid bin Umair, on the authority of Aisha, that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, “prayed six rak’ahs in four prostrations.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"504","Ishaq bin Ibrahim told us, he said: Abba Wakee’, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Ata’, on the authority of Ubaid bin Umair, on the authority of Aisha, She said: “The prayer of the verses is six rak’ahs with four prostrations.”"
"505","Muhammad bin Al-Muthanna told us, he said: Yahya bin Saeed told us, he said: Hisham told us, on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Ata, on the authority of Ubaid bin Umair, on the authority of Aisha, regarding “the prayer of the verses is six rak’ahs, with four prostrations” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"506","Yaqoub bin Ibrahim told us, on the authority of Ibn Ulayya, he said: Sufyan al-Thawri told us, on the authority of Habib bin Abi Thabit, on the authority of Tawoos, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, “prayed eight rak’ahs and four prostrations at the time of an eclipse,” and about an act like that, Abu Abdul Rahman told us: This is a good hadith."
"507","Amr bin Uthman told us, he said: Al-Walid told me, on the authority of Al-Awza’i, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, he said: Kathir bin Abbas told me, on the authority of Abd Allah ibn Abbas said that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, “praised four rak’ahs on the day of the solar eclipse, two rak’ahs, and four prostrations.”"
"508","Muhammad bin Ali bin Al-Hasan bin Shaqiq informed us, he said: Abba Abu Hamza, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Alqamah. On the authority of Abdullah, he said: “I prayed two rak’ahs with the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, while traveling.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"509","Yaqub bin Mahan told us, he said: Anba Al-Qasim bin Malik, on the authority of Ayoub, he is Abu Aidh, on the authority of Bukayr bin Al-Akhnas, on the authority of Mujahid, on the authority of Ibn Abbas said: “God has enjoined prayer on the tongue of your Prophet, four rak’ahs in the city, two rak’ahs when traveling, and one rak’ah in fear.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"510","Ismail bin Masoud told us, he said: Yazid told us, meaning bin Zuray’, he said: Sa’id told us, he said: Qatada told us that Musa bin Salamah He told them that he asked Ibn Abbas, he said: I said: I miss praying in congregation while I am in Batha. What do you think I should pray? He said: “Two rak’ahs of the Sunnah of Abu al-Qasim, may God bless him and grant him peace.”"
"511","Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Aswad informed us, saying: Muhammad ibn Rabi’ah told us, on the authority of Abd al-Hamid ibn Ja’far, on the authority of Yazid ibn Abi Habib On the authority of Arak bin Malik, on the authority of Abdullah bin Abbas, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace: “He stayed in Mecca for fifteen days, praying \Two rak'ahs\"" (Peace Be Upon Him)"""""
"512","Qutaibah bin Saeed told us, he said: Abu Al-Ahwas told us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Harithah bin Wahb Al-Khuza’i, he said: “I prayed With the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, in Mina, he was safer than people were, and the most he performed was two rak’ahs.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"513","Ali bin Khashram told us, he said: Issa told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin Yazid, he said: Uthman prayed In Mina for four days, until this reached Abdullah, and he said: “I prayed two rak’ahs with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace.”"
"514","Amr bin Yazid told us, he said: Bahz bin Asad told us, he said: Shu’bah told us, he said: Salamah told us, he said: I heard Sa’id bin Jubayr, he said: I saw Abdullah bin Omar praying with a group, so he stood and prayed Maghrib three times, then he prayed the evening prayer with two rak’ahs, then he said: Thus I saw the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, make"
"515","Muhammad bin Bashar told us, he said: Yahya bin Saeed told us, on the authority of Sufyan, he said: Abu Bakr bin Abi al-Jahm told me, on the authority of Ubayd Allah bin Abdullah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace: “He prayed with Dhul Qard, and the people lined up behind him in two rows, one row Behind him, the enemy's ranks lined up, so he led a rak'ah of prayer with those behind him, then they departed to their place, and those people came and led them in prayer. rak’ah and did not make up for it.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"516","Ismail bin Masoud told us, he said: Khalid, who is Ibn Al-Harith, told us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Al-Hasan, on the authority of Abu Bakra, that The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “He led the people in fear two rak’ahs, then he gave the salutation, then he led the other people in fear two rak’ahs, then he gave the salutation. So the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, prayed four times.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"517","Imran bin Musa told us, on the authority of Abdul-Warith, he said: Yunus told us, on the authority of Al-Hasan, on the authority of Jabir bin Abdullah, that the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, May God bless him and grant him peace. He led his Companions with the prayer of fear, so he prayed in a group of two rak’ahs, while the others were facing their enemy, then he greeted, then he came. He prayed two rak'ahs with them, then he gave the salutation, so there were four rak'ahs for the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and two rak'ahs for the people.\"" 518"""""
"518","Muhammad ibn Wahb informed us, saying: Muhammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, saying: Abu 'Abd al-Rahim — who is Khalid ibn Abi Yazid — narrated to me, saying: Zayd narrated to me, from Ayyub, from Bukayr ibn al-Akhnas, from Mujahid, from Ibn 'Abbas, who said: ""The resident prayer was prescribed upon the tongue of your Prophet as four (rak'ahs), the travel prayer as two rak'ahs, and the fear prayer as one rak'ah."""""
"519","Muhammad bin Abdul-Ala told us, he said: Al-Mu`tamir told us, he said: I heard Amara bin Ghaziyah, speaking on the authority of Yahya bin Saeed, on the authority of Amer bin Abdullah bin Al-Zubayr, on the authority of Amr bin Sulaym, on the authority of Abu Qatada, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “If one of you enters the mosque, and he should not sit in it until he has prayed two rak’ahs.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"520","519 Qutaibah bin Saeed informed us, on the authority of Sufyan bin Uyaynah, and Yazid, who is Ibn Zuray’, on the authority of Muammar, who is Ibn Rashid Al-Basri, On the authority of Yahya bin Abi Kathir, on the authority of Damdam, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, commanded “to kill the two lions during prayer.” \The serpent and the scorpion\"""""""
"521","520 Qutaibah bin Saeed told us, he said: Malik told us, on the authority of Aamir bin Abdullah bin Al-Zubayr, on the authority of Amr bin Sulaym, on the authority of Abu Qatada said that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, “used to pray while holding an imam, so when he prostrated he would lower it, and when he stood he would raise it.”"
"522","521 Muhammad bin Sadaqa al-Humsi informed us, saying: Muhammad bin Harb told us, on the authority of al-Zubaidi, on the authority of Amer bin Abdullah bin al-Zubayr, On the authority of Amr bin Sulaym, on the authority of Abu Qatada, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace: “He went out to pray while carrying on his shoulders the daughter of Umamah Abu Al-Aas bin Al-Rabi’, and her mother was Zainab, daughter of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. Whenever he bowed, he would place it on his shoulder, and when he finished His prostration took it off his shoulders, and he remained like that until he finished his prayer.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"523","522 Ishaq bin Ibrahim told us, he said: Abba Hatim bin Wardan, said: Burd bin Sinan Abu Al-Ala told us, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Urwa, on the authority of Aisha, said: “I opened the door and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was praying voluntarily with the door facing the Qiblah, so he walked away from to his right, or to his left, then he opened the door and then returned to his place of prayer.”"
"524","523 Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Bazi’ informed us, saying: Abd al-A’la bin Abd al-A’la narrated to us, saying: Ubayd Allah narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Hazim, on the authority of Sahl bin Saad, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, set out to reconcile the Banu Amr bin Awf, and the time for prayer came, so he came The muezzin went to Abu Bakr and ordered him to gather the people and lead them in prayer. Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, came and broke through the rows until he stood in The front row, and the people approached Abu Bakr to call him to the call to prayer to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and Abu Bakr did not turn around during prayer, so when They knew that something had disturbed them during their prayer, so they turned and saw that it was the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and the Messenger of God motioned to him. May God’s prayers and peace be upon him, that is, as you are. Abu Bakr raised his hands and thanked God and praised him for what the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said, then The person who had left behind came back and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, came forward and prayed. When he left, he said to Abu Bakr: “What prevented you if I motioned for you to pray?” Abu Bakr said: It was not appropriate for Ibn Abi Quhafa to lead the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, then he said to the people: “What’s the matter with you? “You have forgiven. Congratulations are only for women.” Then he said: “If anything bothers you in your prayer, then glorify God.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"525","524 Amr bin Ali told us, he said: Abd al-Rahman told us, he said, Zaida told us, on the authority of Ash’ath bin Abi al-Sha’atha’, on the authority of his father, On the authority of Masruq, on the authority of Aisha, she said: I asked the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, about turning away during prayer. He said: “embezzling.” Satan detains him from praying, “Israel opposes him”"
"526","525 Ahmad bin Bakkar Al-Harrani informed us, on the authority of Mukhlid, who is the son of Yazid Al-Harrani, on the authority of Israel, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Abu Attiya al-Kufi, on the authority of Masruq, on the authority of Aisha, who said: I asked the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, about turning around during prayer. He said: “It is A misappropriation by Satan of the servant’s prayer.”"
"527","526 Suwayd bin Nasr told us, he said: Anba Abdullah is Ibn Al-Mubarak, on the authority of Yunus, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, he said: I heard Abu Al-Ahwas, He told us in a gathering of Sa`id ibn al-Musayyab, and Ibn al-Musayyab was sitting, that he heard Abu Dharr say: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said “Indeed, God is facing the servant in his prayer as long as he does not turn away, so if he turns his face away, he will turn away from it.”"
"528","527 Qutaibah bin Saeed told us, he said: Al-Layth told us, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saw He murmured in the direction of the qiblah of the mosque while he was praying in front of the people. He wiped it away, then said when he left: “If one of you is in prayer, then God before his face, so let none of you sigh before his face during prayer.”"
"529","528 Ishaq bin Ibrahim told us, he said: Al-Fadl bin Musa told us, he said: Abdullah bin Saeed bin Abi Hind told us, on the authority of Thawr Ibn Zayd, on the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to look right and left in his prayer, and would not twist \His neck is behind his back.\"""""""
"530","Hanad bin Al-Sirri told us, in his hadith, on the authority of Abu Muawiyah, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Amara bin Umair, on the authority of Abu Muammar, he said: We said: To Khabab: “Did the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, recite at noon and afternoon prayers? He said: Yes. I said: What do you know about? He said: With the disorder of his beard.”"
"531","530 Ali bin Al-Hussein told us, he said: Umayyah told us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, he said: I heard Abdullah bin Yazid, While he was delivering the sermon, he said: Al-Baraa told me, and it is not a lie, that “when they prayed with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and raised Their heads from bowing, they stood up until they saw him prostrating.”"
"532","531 Qutayba bin Saeed and Al-Hussein bin Harith told us, and the wording is his, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Abu Al-Ahwas, on the authority of Abu Dharr said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “If one of you stands for prayer and does not wipe away the pebbles, for mercy will come to him.”"
"533","532 Suwayd bin Nasr told us, he said: Abba Abdullah bin Al-Mubarak, on the authority of Al-Awza’i, on the authority of Yahya bin Abi Kathir, he said: He told me Abu Salamah bin Abdul Rahman said: Mu’aqib told me that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “If you are a doer, then do it.”"
"534","533 Qutayba bin Saeed and Muhammad bin Al-Muthanna told us, saying: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Abu Salamah, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, He said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Tasbih is for men, and clapping is for women.” In the hadith of Ibn Al-Muthanna, regarding prayer, the wording of the hadith Liqtayba (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"535","534 Qutaibah bin Saeed told us, he said: Al-Layth told us, on the authority of Abu Al-Zubayr, on the authority of Jabir, that he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, complained. peace be upon him, so we prayed behind him while he was sitting and Abu Bakr was saying “Allahu Akbar,” and people were hearing him saying “Allahu Akbar,” so he turned to us and saw us standing, so he indicated To us, we sat and we prayed with his prayer, sitting, and when he greeted him, he said: “If you struggle just now, you will do the action of a Persian and the Romans rising up against their kings while they are Sitting, do not do so. Follow your Imams. If he prays standing, they should pray standing, and if he prays sitting, then they should pray sitting.”"
"536","535 Ahmad bin Sulaiman told us, he said: Yahya bin Adam told us, on the authority of Mis’ar, on the authority of Ubayd Allah bin Al-Qibtiyya, on the authority of Jabir bin Samra, he said: We used to pray behind the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and we would say salutations with our hands, and he said: “Why do these people say salutations with their hands as if they were The tails of the horses of the sun. Isn’t it enough for one of them to put his hand on his thigh and then say: Peace be upon you, peace be upon you? (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"537","536 Qutaibah bin Saeed told us, he said: Al-Layth told us, on the authority of Abu Al-Zubayr, on the authority of Jabir, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, sent me He greeted me out of need, then I caught him while he was praying, so I greeted him. He pointed to me, and when he finished he called me and said: “You greeted me just now, and I I pray, but he is then facing toward the east.”"
"538","537 Muhammad bin Al-Ala informed us, saying: Abu Khalid, who is Sulayman bin Hayyan Al-Ahmar, told us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Al-Hakam, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Alqamah, on the authority of Abdullah, on the authority of the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “Indeed, there is busyness in prayer.” Bishr ibn al-Mufaddal disagreed with him. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"539","538 Humayd bin Masada told us, he said: Bishr told us, he said: Shu`bah told us, on the authority of Al-Hakam, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Abdullah, On the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, about a man greeting him while he was praying, he said: “Indeed there is a preoccupation in prayer.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"540","539 Humayd bin Masada told us, he said: Bishr told us, he said: Shu`bah told us, on the authority of Suleiman, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Abdullah, He said: We used to greet the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he was praying and he returned our greetings. When we came to the Abyssinians, we returned, so we greeted him. He did not answer, so we asked him, and he said: “There is a preoccupation in prayer.”"
"541","540 Muhammad bin Bashar told us, he said: Wahb told us, he said: My father told us, he said: Qais bin Saad told us, on the authority of Ata’, on the authority of Muhammad Bin Ali, on the authority of Ammar bin Yasser, that “he greeted the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, while he was praying and he responded to him.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"542","541 Ubayd Allah bin Sa’id Abu Qudamah al-Sarkhasi and Shuaib bin Yusuf Abu Omar al-Nasa’i informed us on the authority of Yahya, meaning bin Sa’id al-Qattan. On the authority of Ibn Abi Orouba, on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Anas ibn Malik, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “What is the matter with people? They raise their eyes to the sky in their prayer, so his statement about that became more severe until he said: Let them cease, or their eyes will be snatched away."
"543","542 Qutayba bin Saeed told us, he said: Al-Fudayl told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Abu Salih, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: The Messenger of God said: May God’s prayers and peace be upon him: “Tasbih is for men, and clapping is for women.”"
"544","Suwayd bin Nasr told us, saying: Anba Abdullah is Ibn Al-Mubarak, on the authority of Hammad bin Salamah, on the authority of Thabit Al-Bunani, on the authority of Mutarrif, On the authority of his father, he said: “I came to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, while he was praying, and his stomach was buzzing like the buzzing of a boiler,” meaning he was crying. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"545","Issa bin Yunus told us, on the authority of Damra, on the authority of Al-Sari bin Yahya, on the authority of Abd al-Karim bin Rashid, on the authority of Ibn al-Shakhir, on the authority of his father, He said: “The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, was heard humming with supplication while he was prostrating, like the hum of a cauldron.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"546","545 Muhammad bin Al-Ala told us, he said: Abu Bakr told us, he said: Abu Ishaq told us, on the authority of Al-Sa’ib bin Malik, on the authority of Abdullah He said: “The sun eclipsed on the day Abraham died, so the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, prayed two rak’ahs, and he began to advance and blow, and then delay.” And it advances and blows, and it retards, and it departed when it departed, and it had become clear.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"547","546 Yahya bin Ayyub told us, he said: Abu Salih told us, he said: Hammad told us, on the authority of Ata’ bin Al-Sa’ib, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abdullah bin Amr, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace: “He was prostrating at the end of his prostration in the prayer of the verses, so he blew at the last prostration, and said: Uff uf uf, then he said: My Lord, did you not promise me that you would not torture them while I was among them? Oh, my Lord, did you not promise me that you would not torture them while they were seeking forgiveness?"
"548","547 Al-Hussein bin Issa Al-Qumsi Al-Bistami told us, saying: Ahmad bin Abi Taybah and Affan bin Sayyar told us, on the authority of Anbasa. Ibn Al-Azhar, on the authority of Salama Ibn Kuhail, on the authority of Kurayb, on the authority of Umm Salamah, who said: The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, passed by a boy of theirs called Rabah. While he was praying, he blew while he was prostrating, and he said to him: O Rabah, do not blow, for whoever blows has already spoken. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"549","548 Muhammad ibn Salamah informed us, on the authority of Ibn Wahb, on the authority of Muawiyah ibn Salih, he said: Rabi’ah ibn Yazid narrated to me, on the authority of Abu Idris. Al-Khawlani, on the authority of Abu Al-Darda’, said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, stood up to pray, and we heard him say: “I seek refuge in God from you,” then he said: I curse you with the curse of God three times,” and he extended his hand as if he was grabbing something. When he finished praying, we said: O Messenger of God, we heard you say during prayer: Something we had not heard you say before, and we saw you stretch out your hand. He said: “Indeed, the enemy of God, Satan, came with a shooting star to put it in My face, so I said: I seek refuge in God from you three times, then I said, I curse you with the curse of God, but he did not delay it three times, then I wanted to take it. By God, had it not been for the call of our brother Solomon, it would have become a document for the children of the people of Medina to play with.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"550","549 Amr bin Uthman told us, he said: Baqiya told us, he said: Al-Zubaidi told me, he said: Al-Zuhri told me, on the authority of Sa’id, on the authority of Abu Huraira, on the authority of the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “While I was standing praying, Satan intercepted me, so I seized him by the throat and strangled him to the point that I I would feel the coldness of his tongue on my thumb. May God have mercy on Suleiman. Had I not called him, he would have been bound and you would be looking at him.” Abu Salamah disagreed with him in his wording. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"551","550 Ishaq bin Ibrahim told us, he said: Anba al-Fadl bin Musa told us, he said: Muhammad bin Amr told us, he said: Abu Salamah told us, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, on the authority of the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “Satan interrupted me while I was praying, so I grabbed a ring and strangled him, until I found “His tongue was cold on my palms, and had it not been for the call of my brother Solomon, he would have been bound as you looked at him.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"552","551 Qutaibah bin Saeed informed us, saying: Abthar, who is Ibn al-Qasim Abu Zubayd al-Kufi, told us, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Al-Musayyab ibn Rafi’, on the authority of Tamim bin Tarfa, on the authority of Jabir bin Samurah, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, went out against us while we were, meaning Rafi’. Our hands in prayer, and he said: “What is the matter with them raising their hands in prayer as if they were the tails of sunken horses? Be still in prayer.”"
"553","552 Qutaibah bin Saeed informed us, he said: Anba Sufyan informed us, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, and Muhammad bin Mansour informed us, on the authority of Sufyan, he said: Al-Zuhri told us, On the authority of Urwa, on the authority of Aisha, that the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, prayed in a khamisah with signs on it. He said: “The signs of this have occupied me. Go with it.” To Abu Jahm, and bring me something that is pure.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"554","552 Kathir ibn Ubaid al-Humsi informed us, saying: Muhammad ibn Harb told us, on the authority of al-Zubaidi, on the authority of al-Zuhri, on the authority of Abu Salamah, that Abu Hurairah, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, got up to pray and we stood up with him, and a Bedouin said while he was in prayer: O God, have mercy on me and Muhammad. And do not be merciful to anyone with us. When the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, greeted him, he said to the Bedouins: “You have become largely petrified. He wants God’s mercy.” He disagreed with him. Sufyan bin Uyaynah (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"555","553 Abdullah bin Muhammad bin Abdul Rahman Al-Zuhri Al-Basri told us, he said: Sufyan told us, he said: Preserve him from Al-Zuhri, he said Saeed told me, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, that a Bedouin entered the mosque and prayed two rak’ahs, then said: O God, have mercy on me and Muhammad, and do not have mercy on us. On Sunday, the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “You have become completely petrified.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"556","Ishaq bin Mansour told us, he said: Abba Muhammad bin Yusuf, he said: Al-Awza’i told us, he said: Yahya bin Abi Kathir told me, on the authority of Hilal bin Abi Maimunah said: Ata bin Yassar told me on the authority of Muawiyah bin Al-Hakam Al-Sulami, who said: While I was with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace He said the salaam during prayer, when a man from among the people sneezed, and I said: May God have mercy on you. Then the people looked away from me with their eyes, and I said: How heavy is the illiterate that you have? Are you looking at me? He said: The people struck their hands on their thighs, and when I saw them silence me, I remained silent. When the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, left He called me by my father and my mother. He did not hit me, nor curse me, nor curse me. I have never seen a teacher before him or after him with better teaching than him. He said: “Indeed In this prayer of ours, nothing people say is appropriate. Rather, it is glorification, glorification, and recitation of the Qur’an.” Then I showed my spoils, and he mentioned the hadith. Brief (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"557","Suwayd bin Nasr informed us, saying: Anba Abdullah, on the authority of Ismail bin Abi Khalid, on the authority of Al-Harith bin Shubail, on the authority of Abu Amr Al-Shaybani, on the authority of Zayd bin Arqam, said: “During the time of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, one of us was speaking to his companion during prayer about his need, until the verse came down. This verse: “Guard the prayers and the middle prayer and stand before God in obedience.” At that time we were commanded to remain silent. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"558","556 Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Ammar Al-Mawsili informed us, saying: Ibn Abi Ghaniyah and Al-Qasim told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Al-Zubayr bin Adi, on the authority of Kulthum, on the authority of Abdullah bin Masoud, and this is the hadith of Al-Qasim, he said: I used to come to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, while he was praying. So I greeted him, and he responded to me. So I went to him and greeted him while he was praying, but he did not respond to me. When he greeted, he pointed to the people and said: “Indeed, God. That is to say, it was introduced into the prayer that you should not speak except in the remembrance of God, and that is not befitting for you, and that you should stand up to God in obedience.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"559","557 Al-Hussein bin Harith told us, he said: Abba Sufyan, on the authority of Asim, on the authority of Abu Wael, on the authority of Ibn Masoud, he said: We used to greet the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him. May God bless him and grant him peace, and he returned our greetings, until we came from the land of Abyssinia, so I greeted him, but he did not respond to me, so he took me from what was near and after. So I sat until he finished the prayer. He said: “Indeed, God creates His command whatever He wishes, and He has created His command not to speak during the prayer.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"560","558 Suleiman bin Ubayd Allah Al-Ghaylani told us, he said: Bahz told us, he said: Shu’bah told us, on the authority of Saad bin Ibrahim, that he heard Abu Salamah, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, narrates that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, prayed two rak’ahs of noon prayer and then gave the salutation. They said: The prayer has been shortened. So he stood up and prayed two rak’ahs, then said the salaam, then prostrated two prostrations.” Abu Abd al-Rahman said: I do not know of anyone who mentioned this on the authority of Abu Salamah. The hadith “Then he prostrated two prostrations” is not Saad."
"561","559 Issa bin Hammad informed us, saying: Anba Al-Layth, on the authority of Yazid bin Abi Habib, on the authority of Imran bin Abi Anas, on the authority of Abu Salamah, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, prayed one day and said the salaam in two rak’ahs, then he departed, and Dhu al-Shamalayn overtook him and said: O Messenger of By God, did the prayer decrease or did I forget? He said: The prayer did not decrease, nor did I forget. He said: Yes, by the One who sent you with the truth, the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said. He said: “Did he do the two rak’ahs?” They said, “Yes.” So he led the people in prayer two rak’ahs."
"562","560 Ibrahim bin Yaqoub told us, he said: Al-Hasan bin Musa told us, he said: Shayban told us, he said: Yahya bin Abi Kathir told us, On the authority of Abu Salamah, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: “While I was praying the noon prayer with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, greeted He prayed the salutation after two rak'ahs, then a man from Banu Sulaym stood up and said: O Messenger of God, did you shorten the prayer or did you forget? So the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said He, peace and blessings be upon him: It was not shortened, and I have not forgotten. He said: O Messenger of God, I only prayed two rak’ahs. The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: What is more worthy of that? He said: “Yes.” They said: “Yes.” So he prayed two rak’ahs with them."
"563","561 Ahmad bin Saeed told us, he said: Hibban bin Hilal told us, he said: Aban bin Yazid Al-Attar told us, he said: Yahya told me Ibn Abi Kathir said: Abu Salamah Ibn Abd al-Rahman told me, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, “may God bless him and grant him peace.” He led his companions and said the salutation in two rak'ahs, then a man called Dhul-Yadin, who had long hands, said: O Messenger of God, did you shorten the prayer or did you forget? He said: The prayer was not short and I did not forget. He said: What did the two hands say? They said: He spoke the truth, so he prayed two rak’ahs with them."
"564","562 Harun bin Musa told us, he said: Abu Damra told us, on the authority of Yunus, on the authority of Ibn Shihab, he said: Abu Salamah told me, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: “The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, forgot and said the salutation in two prostrations, so Dhu al-Shamalayn said to him: Did you shorten the prayer or did you forget, O Messenger? God? The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Did those with two hands speak the truth? They said: Yes, so the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, stood up and completed the prayer."
"565","563 Muhammad bin Rafi’ told us, he said: Abd al-Razzaq told us, Abba Muammar said, on the authority of al-Zuhri, on the authority of Abu Salamah bin Abdul Rahman, On the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: “The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, prayed the noon or afternoon prayer, and he gave the salutation in two rak’ahs. Then Dhu al-Shimalayn bin Amr: Was the prayer shortened or was it forgotten? Then the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: What did the two hands say? They said: He spoke the truth, O Prophet of God, so complete them? The two rak’ahs that were shortened.” Abu Dawud told us, he said: Ya’qub told us, he said: My father told us, on the authority of Salih, on the authority of Ibn Shihab, that Abu Bakr bin Suleiman bin Abi Hathamah told him that he had heard that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace: “He prayed two rak’ahs, so he said to him Dhu al-Shamalayn and something similar. Ibn Shihab said: This news was told to me by Sa`id bin al-Musayyab, on the authority of Abu Hurairah. He said: And Abu told him. Salama bin Abdul Rahman, Abu Bakr bin Abdul Rahman bin Al Harith, who is Ibn Hisham, and Ubaid Allah bin Abdullah, Anba Muhammad Ibn Abdullah Ibn Abd al-Hakam, on the authority of Shuaib, who said: Anba al-Layth reported, on the authority of Uqail, who said: Ibn Shihab told me, on the authority of Sa`id and Abu Salamah And Abu Bakr bin Abdul Rahman, and Ibn Abi Hathamah, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, that “the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, did not prostrate, On that day, before the greeting of peace, or after it.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"566","564 Suwayd bin Nasr informed us, he said: Abba Abdullah, on the authority of Ikrimah bin Ammar, he said: Abba Damm bin Jus, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace: “He prostrated the two prostrations of forgetfulness while sitting, then he greeted,” he mentioned it in the hadith of Dhul-Yadin."
"567","565 Ibrahim bin Yaqoub told us, he said: Al-Hasan bin Musa told me, he said: Anba Shaiban, he said: Yahya bin Abi Kathir told us, Damm bin Jus told me that he heard Abu Hurairah say: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, prostrated two prostrations.”"
"568","566 Amr bin Sawad bin Al-Aswad bin Amr told us, he said: Abdullah bin Wahb informed us, he said: Al-Layth bin Saad informed us, on the authority of Yazid bin Abu Habib, on the authority of Ja’far bin Rabi’ah, on the authority of Arak bin Malik, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace: “He prostrated on the day The one with two hands prostrated after the salutation.” Amr ibn Sawad informed us, saying: Ibn Wahb informed us, he said: Amr ibn al-Harith informed us, he said: Tell me Qatada, on the authority of Muhammad ibn Sirin, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, on the authority of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, with a similar example. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"569","567 Muhammad bin Salamah told us, he said: Anba Ibn al-Qasim, on the authority of Malik, he said: Ayoub told me, on the authority of Muhammad bin Sirin, on the authority of Abu Hurairah The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, left after two days, and Dhu al-Yadin said to him: Have you shortened the prayer, or have you forgotten, O Messenger of God? The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: Did the one with the two hands give in charity? The people said: Yes, so the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, stood up and prayed two times, then he prayed two times. He said the salaam, then he said “Allahu Akbar”, so he prostrated like his prostration, or longer, then he raised his head, then he prostrated like his prostration, or longer, then he raised his head.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"570","568 Humayd bin Masada told us, he said: Yazid told us, and he is bin Zurai’, he said: Ibn Aoun told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Sirin, he said: Abu Hurairah said: The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, led with us one of the evening prayers. Abu Hurairah said: But I forgot. He said: “So he led with us.” He prayed two rak'ahs, then he said the salutation, then he went to a piece of wood displayed in the mosque, and said with his hand on it as if he was angry, and the two dragons came out of the The doors of the mosque, and they said: Has the prayer been short? And among the people were Abu Bakr and Omar, who were afraid to speak to him, and among the people was a man with long hands. He said: He was called Dhul-Yadin. He said: O Messenger of God, did you forget or was the prayer shortened? He said: I did not forget, and the prayer was not shortened. He said: And he said: Either? The two hands said: Yes, so he came and the one who had left prayed, then he said the takbir, then he prostrated like his prostration, or longer, then he rose. \ (Peace Be Upon Him)"""""
"571","569 Qutaibah bin Saeed informed us, on the authority of Malik, on the authority of Dawud bin Al-Husayn, on the authority of Abu Sufyan, the client of Ibn Abi Ahmad, who said: I heard Abu Hurairah said: “The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, led the afternoon prayer with us, and he gave the salutation in two rak’ahs, then Dhu al-Yadin stood up and said: Was the prayer shortened, O Messenger of God, or did you forget? Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: All of that did not happen, so he said: Some of that happened, O Messenger. So the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, approached the people and said: Did Dhu al-Din speak the truth? They said: Yes, so the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, completed it. He (peace and blessings of Allaah be upon him) performed the remainder of the prayer, then he prostrated two prostrations, while he was sitting after the salutation.”"
"572","570 Abu Al-Ash’ath told us, on the authority of Yazid bin Zuray’, he said: Khalid Al-Hadha’ told us, on the authority of Abu Qilaba, on the authority of Abu Al-Muhallab, on the authority of Imran bin Al-Hussein said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, greeted him after three rak’ahs of the afternoon prayer. He entered and a man called him stood up to him. Al-Kharbaq, and he said: Prayer, O Messenger of God, so he went out angrily, dragging his cloak, and said: Is that true? They said: Yes, so he got up and prayed that rak’ah. Then he saluted, then he prostrated as she prostrated, then he saluted.”"
"573","Ahmad bin Saeed told us, he said: Wahb bin Jarir told us, he said: My father told us, he said: I heard Al-A’mash, speaking on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Alqamah, on the authority of Abdullah, that “he prayed five times, then he mentioned the sixth time and sat down, and prostrated two prostrations,” and said: This is what the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, did. Peace be upon him"
"574","572 Abdah bin Abd al-Rahim told us, he said: Abba Ibn Shumail, he said: Shu`bah narrated to us, on the authority of al-Hakam, and Mughirah, on the authority of Ibrahim, On the authority of Alqamah, on the authority of Abdullah, on the authority of the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, that “he led them in the noon prayer five times, and they said: You prayed five times,” so he prostrated. “Two prostrations, after he said the salutation while he was sitting.” Anba Qutaybah bin Sa’id said: Abu Awanah told us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Ibrahim, that The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, prayed as a messenger (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"575","573 Suwayd bin Nasr informed us, saying: Anba Abdullah, on the authority of Abu Bakr Al-Nahshali, on the authority of Abdul Rahman bin Al-Aswad, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abdullah, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace: “He prayed one of the evening prayers as five times, and it was said to him: Should I add more to the prayer? He said: What is that? They said: “I prayed five times, and he said: I am only a human being. I forget as you forget, and I remember as you remember.” So he prostrated two prostrations and then turned away."
"576","574 Al-Hasan bin Ismail bin Sulayman informed us, saying: Abba Fudayl, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Alqamah, on the authority of Abdullah, He said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, prayed a prayer, adding or subtracting from it. When he gave the salutation, we said: O Prophet of God, did anything happen in the prayer? He said: What is that? He said: So we mentioned to him what he had done, so he bent his leg and faced the Qiblah and prostrated the two prostrations of forgetfulness, then he turned to us. On his face, he said: “If something had happened during prayer, I would have informed you about it.” Then he said: “I am only human, I forget just as you forget, so which of you is not He forgot something in his prayer, so let him check what he thinks is correct, then he should say the salutation, then perform the two prostrations of forgetfulness.” Shaqiq ibn Salamah Abu Wael, so he based his investigation on Abdullah’s statement. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"577","575 Muhammad bin Bashar told us, he said: Muhammad bin Ja’far Ghandar told us, he said: Shu’bah told us, on the authority of Al-Hakam, he said: I heard Aba Wael, narrating, on the authority of Abdullah, said: “If one of you is distracted in prayer, let him strive for what is right, and prostrate two prostrations while sitting after \empties\"" (Peace Be Upon Him)"""""
"578","576 Imran bin Yazid told us, he said: Abdul Aziz told us, he said: Zayd bin Aslam told us, on the authority of Ata’ bin Yasar, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “If one of you doubts about his prayer and does not know whether he prayed three or four, let him stand.” Let him kneel, meaning one rak'ah, and prostrate two prostrations. If it is the fifth, then he will intercede for them with two prostrations, and if it is the fourth, then two prostrations. To discourage Satan.”"
"579","577 Yahya bin Habib bin Arabi told us, he said: Khaled told us, he is Ibn Al-Harith, on the authority of Ibn Ajlan, on the authority of Zayd bin Aslam, On the authority of Ata’, on the authority of Abu Sa’id, on the authority of the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, who said: “If one of you doubts about his prayer, let him eliminate doubt and remain certain. Then when he is completely awake, let him prostrate two prostrations while sitting.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"580","578 Ismail bin Masoud told us, he said: Yahya bin Muhammad bin Qais Abu Zukair told us, on the authority of Zayd bin Aslam, on the authority of Ata’ Ibn Yasar, on the authority of Abu Saeed Al-Khudri, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “If one of you is in doubt and does not know whether to pray three times, or Four, then let him pray a complete rak’ah, then perform two prostrations while sitting. If the rak’ah is a fifth, he should intercede with these two prostrations. It was the fourth time, and they were a temptation for Satan.” Iyad bin Hilal disagreed with him in his wording. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"581","579 Ismail bin Masoud told us, he said: Khalid, meaning Ibn Al-Harith, told us, he said: Hisham, who is Al-Dastawi, told us, on the authority of Yahya is Ibn Abi Kathir, on the authority of Iyad, who said: I asked Abu Sa’id Al-Khudri, I said: One of us prays and does not know how many times he has prayed, he said: He said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace: “If one of you prays and does not know how many times he has prayed, let him prostrate twice while sitting.”"
"582","280 Ibrahim bin Yaqoub told us, he said: Al-Hasan bin Musa told us, he said: Shayban told us, on the authority of Yahya, he said: Iyad bin Musa told me, Hilal Al-Ansari, said: I heard Abu Saeed Al-Khudri, saying: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “If one of you prays and forgets,” or He said: “He does not know whether to increase or decrease, so let him prostrate two prostrations while sitting.”"
"583","581 Shuaib bin Shuaib bin Ishaq told us, he said: Abdul Wahhab told us, he said: Shuaib told us, he said: Al-Awza’i told us, he said: Yahya told me that Iyad bin Hilal told him, he said: I heard Abu Sa`id saying: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “If he forgets One of you is in his prayer and does not know whether to add more or less, so let him prostrate two prostrations while he is sitting."
"584","582 Amr bin Uthman informed us, on the authority of Baqiya, on the authority of Al-Awza’i, on the authority of Yahya, that Iyad bin Hilal narrated to him, saying: I heard Abu Saeed Al-Khudri says: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “If one of you makes a mistake in his prayer and does not know whether he added more or less, let him prostrate.” He prostrated two times while he was sitting. Ikrimah bin Ammar disagreed with them."
"585","583 Ishaq bin Mansour told us, he said: Abba Omar bin Yunus told us, he said: Ikrimah bin Ammar told us, he said: Yahya told us, he said: Hilal bin Iyad Al-Ansari narrated to me, he said: Abu Sa’id Al-Khudri narrated to me, he said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “When he prays “If one of you does not know whether he added more or less, let him prostrate two prostrations while sitting, then say the salutation.”"
"586","584 Imran bin Yazid told us, he said: Ismail bin Abdullah, he is Ibn Sama’ah, told us, on the authority of Al-Awza’i, he said: he told me Al-Zuhri and Yahya, on the authority of Abu Salamah, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “If Satan confuses “If one of you is praying and does not know whether he has prayed three times or four, let him prostrate two prostrations while sitting.”"
"587","585 Qutayba bin Saeed informed us, on the authority of Malik, on the authority of Ibn Shihab, on the authority of Abu Salamah, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace He, peace and blessings be upon him, said: “When one of you stands to pray, Satan comes to him and overwhelms him to the point that he does not know how many times he has prayed. Let him prostrate two prostrations while sitting.”"
"588","586 Suwayd bin Nasr told us, he said: Abba Abdullah, who is Ibn al-Mubarak, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, he said: Abdullah bin Musafa’ told me, On the authority of Utba bin Muhammad bin Al-Harith, on the authority of Abdullah bin Jafar, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Whoever doubts his prayer Let him prostrate two prostrations after he has saluted.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"589","587 Al-Rabi’ bin Sulayman told us, he said: Shuaib bin Al-Layth told us, he said: Al-Layth told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ajlan, on the authority of Muhammad bin Yusuf, the client of Uthman, on the authority of His father, that Muawiyah prayed in front of them, and he stood up during the prayer while sitting, and the people said the Subhanahu, so he completed his standing, then he prostrated with us two prostrations while he was sitting. After he completed the prayer, then he sat on the pulpit and said: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying: “Whoever forgets anything of his prayer Let him prostrate like these two prostrations.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"590","Muhammad ibn Adam informed us, on the authority of Hafs, who is Ibn Ghayath, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Alqamah, on the authority of Abdullah, that the Prophet prayed May God bless him and grant him peace: “He greeted, then he spoke, then he prostrated the two prostrations of forgetfulness.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"591","590 Mahmoud bin Ghaylan told us, he said: Wahb bin Jarir told us, he said: Shu’bah told us, on the authority of Abd Rabbuh bin Sa’id, on the authority of Muhammad Ibn Yahya Ibn Hibban, on the authority of Malik Ibn Buhaynah, that he “prayed with the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he stood up in the Shafi’ who wanted to sit.” Therein, we glorified Him, and he went on, then he prostrated two prostrations.” Abu Abdul Rahman told us: This is wrong, but the correct thing is Abdullah bin Malik bin Buhayna. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"592","591 Abu Dawud told us, he said: Wahb told us, he said: Shu’bah told us, on the authority of Yahya bin Sa’id, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman al-Araj, On the authority of Ibn Buhaynah, that the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, “prayed and stood up for the two rak’ahs, so they said the rosary and he went on, and when he finished his prayer he prostrated two prostrations.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"593","592 Yahya bin Habib bin Arabi told us, he said: Hammad told us, on the authority of Yahya, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman al-Araj, on the authority of Ibn Buhaynah, The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, prayed and stood up during the Shaf’ in which he wanted to sit, so he continued in his prayer, until when it was at the end of his prayer, He prostrated two prostrations before he said the salutation, then he saluted.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"594","593 Suwayd bin Nasr informed us, saying: Abba Abdullah, on the authority of Yahya bin Saeed, that Abd al-Rahman bin Hurmuz informed him, about Abdullah bin Malik bin Buhaynah said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, stood up in the two rak’ahs of the noon prayer, so he remained standing, then prostrated.” Two prostrations, then the salutation.” Abu Abd al-Rahman said: This is correct."
"595","594 Qutaibah bin Saeed told us, on the authority of Malik, on the authority of Ibn Shihab, on the authority of Al-Araj, on the authority of Abdullah bin Buhayna, he said: “He prayed for us The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, prayed two rak’ahs, then he stood up and did not sit down, so the people stood up with him. When he finished his prayer and we saw his greeting, he said “Allah is Great” and prostrated. He prostrated two times while he was sitting before the salutation, then he saluted.”"
"596","595 Ismail bin Masoud told us, he said: Khaled told us, he said: Hisham told us, on the authority of Yahya, he said: Abdul Rahman told me Al-Araj, and Anba Suleiman bin Salam, he said: Anba Al-Nadr, he said: Anba Hisham, on the authority of Yahya, on the authority of Abdul Rahman Al-Araj, on the authority of Abdullah Ibn Malik Ibn Buhayna said that “the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, testified when he stood up from the two rak’ahs and forgot to sit down, so he continued to stand So he prostrated two prostrations after he finished his prayer.”"
"597","596 Abu Bakr bin Ishaq informed us, saying: Abu Zayd al-Harawi Sa’id bin al-Rabi’ informed us, saying: Ali bin al-Mubarak told me, on the authority of Yahya bin Abi Kathir, on the authority of Damdam bin Jaws, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace: “He prayed the noon prayer, so he stood up in He did not sit the first two rak’ahs, even when it was at the end of his prayer, so he prostrated two prostrations before he said the salutation, then he saluted.”"
"598","597 Ahmad bin Amr told us, he said: Ibn Wahb informed us, he said: Amr, Yunus, and Al-Layth told me that Ibn Shihab told them On the authority of Abd al-Rahman al-Araj, that Abd Allah ibn Buhaynah told him that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, “stood up at two o’clock in the afternoon.” He did not sit, and when he had finished his prayer, he prostrated two prostrations, saying “Allahu Akbar” in each prostration, while he was sitting, before he said the salutation, and the people prostrated them with him at a place He did not forget to sit.”"
"599","599 Amr bin Hisham told us, he said: Muhammad bin Salamah told us, on the authority of Khusayf, on the authority of Abu Ubaidah, on the authority of his father, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. He, peace and blessings of God be upon him, said: “If you were in prayer and doubted three or four times, and most likely your doubts were four times, you recited the tashahhud, then you prostrated before You said the salaam, then you also testified, then you said the salaam.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"600","600 Muhammad bin Yahya bin Abdullah told us, he said: Muhammad bin Abdullah Al-Ansari told us, he said: Ash’ath told me he is Ibn Abd al-Malik, on the authority of Muhammad ibn Sirin, on the authority of Khaled al-Hadha, on the authority of Abu Qalaba, on the authority of Abu al-Muhallab, on the authority of Imran, that the Prophet prayed May God bless him and grant him peace. “He led them in prayer for a short period of time, then prostrated and then saluted.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"601","601 Yahya bin Habib bin Arabi told us, he said: Hammad told us, he said: Khaled told us, on the authority of Abu Qalaba, on the authority of Abu Al-Muhallab, On the authority of Imran bin Husayn, that the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him: “He prayed three rak’ahs and then gave salutations. Al-Kharbaq said: You prayed three times, so he led the rak’ah with them.” Then he said the salaam, then he prostrated the two prostrations of forgetfulness, then he said the salaam.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"602","Ahmad bin Sulaiman told us, he said: Yahya bin Adam told us, he said: Malik, who is Ibn Mughal, told us, on the authority of Talha bin Musarrif, On the authority of Zayd bin Wahb, on the authority of Hudhayfah, that he saw a man praying, so he became humble, and Hudhayfah said to him: “How long have you been praying this prayer?” He said: Forty years ago, he said: “You have not prayed for forty years, and if you had died while praying this prayer, you would have died unlike the nature of Muhammad, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him.” And he greeted, then he said: “The man has fear, completes his prayers, and does good.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"603","Ahmad bin Sulaiman Al-Rahwi told us, he said: Yazid told us, he said: Abba Shu’bah, on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Anas, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace May God bless him and grant him peace, “He is one of the people who performs the prayer most easily in completion.”"
"604","605 Muhammad ibn Abd al-Ala al-San’ani told us, he said: Khaled told us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Hamza, he said: I heard Anas, saying: “ I have never prayed behind a person with a lighter prayer than the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"605","606 Amr bin Ali told us, he said: Yahya, who is Al-Qattan, told us, he said: Ubayd Allah told us, he said: Saeed bin Abi Saeed told me, On the authority of Omar bin Abi Bakr bin Abdul Rahman, on the authority of his father, that Ammar bin Yasser said: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying: “A man prays, and perhaps he only has a tenth of it, or a ninth of it, or an eighth of it, or a seventh of his prayer until he reaches the last number.” \"" 606"""""
"606","Qutaybah ibn Sa'id informed us, saying: Bakr — who is ibn Mudad — narrated to us, from Ibn 'Ajlan, from Sa'id — who is ibn Abi Sa'id al-Maqburi — from 'Umar ibn al-Hakam, from 'Abdullah ibn 'Anamah, that 'Ammar ibn Yasir said: ""I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: 'A man may finish his prayer while only a tenth of it is recorded for him, or a ninth, or an eighth, or a seventh, or a sixth, or a fifth, or a quarter, or a third, or a half.'"""""
"607","608 Muhammad bin Salamah Al-Masry told us, he said: Ibn Wahb told us, on the authority of Amr bin Al-Harith, on the authority of Sa’id bin Abi Hilal, on the authority of Omar Ibn Al-Hakam Al-Ansari, on the authority of Abu Al-Yusr, the companion of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Among you are those who He prays the complete prayer, and among you is he who prays the half, the third, the quarter, and the fifth, until he reaches the tenth.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"608","609 Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Abdul-Hakam told us, on the authority of Shuaib, he said: Al-Layth told us, he said: Khalid told us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Hilal, On the authority of Sa’id bin Abi Sa’id al-Maqbari, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, on the authority of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, “The servant prays and does not Except a tenth of his prayers will be recorded for him, then a ninth, then an eighth, then a seventh, until his prayers are recorded as complete.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"609","610 Suwayd bin Nasr informed us, saying: Anba Abdullah is Ibn al-Mubarak, on the authority of Laith bin Sa’d, he said: Abd Rabbuh bin Sa’id narrated to me. On the authority of Imran bin Abi Anas, on the authority of Abdullah bin Nafi’ bin Al-Amiya, on the authority of Rabi’ah bin Al-Harith, on the authority of Al-Fadl bin Al-Abbas, he said : The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Prayer is two by two. You recite the Tashahhud in every two rak’ahs, and you supplicate and submit with humility, and remain still and lower your hands.” He says: “You raise them up to your Lord, facing Your face with their bellies, and say: O Lord, O Lord, whoever has not done such-and-such and such-and-such.” It means a prematurity, the other side of which is a stroke."
"610","611 Ishaq bin Ibrahim told us, he said: Anba Sa’id bin Amir, he said: Shu’bah told us, on the authority of Abd Rabbuh bin Sa’id, on the authority of Anas Ibn Abi Anas, on the authority of Abdullah Ibn Nafi’, on the authority of Abdullah Ibn Al-Harith, on the authority of Al-Muttalib, on the authority of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, He said: “Prayer is two by two, and you recite the Tashahhud in every two rak’ahs, and you frown and remain still and fold your hands, and say: Oh God, O God. Whoever does not do that.” That is a prematurity.”"
"611","Ismail bin Masoud told us, he said: Khalid told us, on the authority of Shu`bah, on the authority of Suleiman, he said: I heard Ibrahim speaking, on the authority of Alqamah And the black one is that they were with Abdullah in his house, so he said: Did these people pray? They said: Yes, so he led them in front of them, then he stood between them without calling to prayer or iqamah, and said: “If there are three of you, then do thus, and if there are More than that, let one of you lead you in prayer, and spread his palms and thighs, as if I am looking at the different fingers of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. May God bless him and grant him peace.”"
"612","Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Rafi’ told us, he said: Yahya bin Adam told us, he said: Mufaddal bin Muhalhalil told us, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Ibrahim, On the authority of Alqamah and Al-Aswad, they entered upon Abdullah. He said: “Did these people pray behind you?” They said: We said: No. He said: “So they prayed.” He said: So he stood between us and then prayed. When we bowed, We placed our hands on the knees to take pleasure in them, and behold, he applied them. When he finished the prayer, he said: “There will be princes who will kill the prayer and stifle it.” The east of the dead, and that is the prayer of one who finds no place and who is worse than the heat. So they prayed the prayer at its appointed time and prayed the rosary with them, so when There were three of you, then all of you prayed, and if there were more of you, let one of you lead you, and when one of you bowed, let him put his hands between his knees. Or between his thighs, and he gave birth, and it is as if I were looking at the differences in the fingers of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"613","Ahmad bin Sa`id al-Marwazi al-Rabbati told us, saying: Abd al-Rahman bin Abdullah told us, saying: Amr informed us, on the authority of al-Zubayr, and he Ibn Adiy, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Al-Aswad, and Alqamah, they said: “We prayed with Abdullah bin Masoud in his house, and he stood between us and placed us. Meaning, our hands, on our knees, so he took them off and crossed our fingers, and said: I saw the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, doing it."
"614","615 Nuh ibn Habib al-Qumsi informed us, saying: Ibn Idris told us, on the authority of Asim ibn Kulayb, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Aswad, on the authority of Alqamah, on the authority of Abdullah, said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, taught us the prayer. So he stood up and said “Allahu Akbar.” When he wanted to bow, he placed his hands between his hands. His knees, and he bowed.” This reached Sa’d, and he said: “You are right, my brother. We were doing this, then we were ordered to do this,” meaning to hold on to the knees."
"615","Qutaibah bin Sa’id told us, he said: Abu Awanah told us, on the authority of Abu Ya’four, on the authority of Mus’ab bin Sa’d, he said: I prayed next to my father He said: “I put my hands between my knees, and he said to me: ‘Strike your palms on your knees.’” He said: Then I did that again, so he struck my hands. And he said: “We have been forbidden from this, and we have been commanded to strike with the palms on the knees.”"
"616","Amr bin Ali told us, he said: Yahya told us, on the authority of Ismail, on the authority of Al-Zubayr bin Adiy, on the authority of Musab bin Saad, he said: I kneeled So I applied, and my father said: “This is something we used to do, then we rose to the knees.”"
"617","Muhammad ibn Bashshar informed us, saying: Abu Dawud narrated to me, saying: Shu'bah narrated to us, from al-A'mash, from Ibrahim, from Abu 'Abd al-Rahman, from 'Umar, who said: ""The placing of the knees (in prostration) was made a Sunnah for you, so hold fast to the knees."""""
"618","Suwayd bin Nasr told us, he said: Anba Abdullah, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Abu Husayn, on the authority of Abu Abdul Rahman al-Salami, he said: Omar said: As for the Sunnah, it is to follow suit.”"
"619","620 Hanad bin Al-Sari told us, in his hadith, on the authority of Abu Al-Ahwas, on the authority of Ata’, on the authority of Salim, who said: We came to Abu Masoud and said to him: He told us about the prayer of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace: “So he stood up in front of us and said “Allahu Akbar,” and when he bowed, he placed his palms on his knees, and made He placed his fingers lower than that, and brought his elbows together until everything was level with him, then he said: God hears whoever praises Him, so he stood up until everything was level. \Something of it\"""""""
"620","621 Ahmad bin Suleiman Al-Rahawi told us, he said: Husayn told us, on the authority of Zaida, on the authority of Ata, on the authority of Salem Abi Abdullah, on the authority of Uqba bin Amr said: “Shall I not pray for you as I saw the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, praying?” So we said: “Yes.” So he stood up and when he bowed down he placed He placed his palms on his knees, put his fingers behind his knees, and touched his armpits until everything was stable, then he raised his head and stood Until everything on him settled, then he prostrated and wiped his armpits until everything on him settled, then he sat until everything on him settled, then he made Likewise, four rak'ahs. Then he said: This is how I saw the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, praying, and this is how he used to lead us in prayer."
"621","622 Ya’qub bin Ibrahim told us, on the authority of Ibn Ulayya, on the authority of Ata’ bin Al-Sa’ib, on the authority of Salim Al-Barrad, he said: Abu Masoud said He is the Ansari: “Shall I not show you how the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to pray?” So we said: “Yes,” so he got up and said “Allahu Akbar.” His armpits until when everything was settled, he raised his head and prayed four rak'ahs like this, and said: This is how I saw the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. And he greeted and prayed.”"
"622","623 Muhammad bin Bashar told us, he said: Yahya told us, he said: Abd al-Hamid bin Ja’far told us, he said: Muhammad bin Amr bin told me. Ata’, on the authority of Abu Humaid al-Sa’idi, who said: The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, “when he bowed, he would stand up straight and would not hold his head straight, nor would he be persuaded.” And he put his hands on his knees.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"623","624 Ubayd Allah ibn Sa`id al-Sarkhasi Abu Qudamah informed us, saying: Hammad ibn Masada told us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Muhammad, on the authority of Ubaidah, on the authority of Ali, who said: The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, forbade me, “about the cloth, the silk, and the gold ring, and that I should recite while I bowing” and he said again “and to recite bowing” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"624","625 Ubayd Allah bin Saeed told us, he said: Yahya bin Saeed told us, he said: On the authority of Ibn Ajlan, on the authority of Ibrahim bin Abdullah bin Hunayn, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, on the authority of Ali, he said: The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, forbade me from wearing a gold ring, and from reciting while bowing. “And about the hardwood and the safflower.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"625","626 Al-Hasan bin Dawud Al-Mankadri informed us, saying: Abba Ibn Abi Fudaik, on the authority of Al-Dahhak bin Uthman, on the authority of Ibrahim bin Hunayn, on the authority of His father, on the authority of Abdullah bin Abbas, on the authority of Ali, who is Ibn Abi Talib, said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, forbade me, and I do not say “We forbid you from wearing gold seals, from wearing a religious garment, from wearing cloth and turbans, and from reciting while bowing.”"
"626","627 Issa bin Hammad bin Zaghbah told us, on the authority of Al-Layth, on the authority of Yazid, that Ibrahim bin Abdullah bin Hunayn told him, that His father told him that he heard Ali say: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, forbade me from wearing a gold ring and wearing a bow. And the rainforest, and the recitation of the Qur’an, while I was bowing.”"
"627","629 Qutayba bin Saeed informed us, on the authority of Malik, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibrahim bin Abdullah bin Hunayn, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Ali, He said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, forbade me “from wearing coarse and fine cloth, from stamping gold, and from reciting while bowing.”"
"628","630 Qutaibah bin Saeed informed us, saying: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Sulayman bin Suhaim, on the authority of Ibrahim bin Abdullah bin Ma’abad bin Abbas, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, revealed the curtain, and the people were in rows behind Abu Bakr, and he said: O people, “Nothing remains of the glad tidings of prophecy except the good vision, which the Muslim will see or it will be seen for him.” Then he said: “But I have been forbidden to Recite while bowing or prostrating. As for bowing, glorify the Lord, and as for prostration, be diligent in supplication, on the hope that it will be answered.”"
"629","631 Ishaq bin Ibrahim bin Rahwayh informed us, saying: Abba Abu Muawiyah, saying: Al-A’mash told us, on the authority of Saad bin Ubaidah, on the authority of Al-Mustarid bin Al-Ahnaf, on the authority of Silah bin Zufar, on the authority of Hudhayfah, said: “I prayed with the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, and he kneeled down and said: In his bowing: “Glory be to my Lord the Great,” and in his prostration: “Glory be to my Lord, the Most High.”"
"630","632 Ismail bin Masoud told us, he said: Khaled told us, and Yazid, they said: Shu’bah told us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Abu Ad-Duha, on the authority of Stolen, on the authority of Aisha, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, would often say in his bowing and prostration: Glory be to You, our Lord. And with Your praise, O God, forgive me.”"
"631","633 Muhammad bin Abdul-Ala told us, he said: Khalid told us, he said: Shu’bah told us, he said: Qatada told me, on the authority of Mutarrif, On the authority of Aisha, she said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to say while bowing: Glory be to the Holy One, Lord of the angels and the spirit.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"632","634 Amr bin Ali told us, he said: Abd al-Rahman bin Mahdi told us, he said: Abd al-Aziz bin Abi Salamah told us, he said: he told me My uncle Al-Majishun bin Abi Salamah, on the authority of Abdul Rahman Al-Araj, on the authority of Ubayd Allah bin Abi Rafi’, on the authority of Ali bin Abi Talib, that the Messenger God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, was: “When he bowed, he would say: O God, for You I kneel, and for You I submit, and in You I believe, my hearing and my sight submit to You, And my bones, and my brain, and my nerves.”"
"633","635 Yahya bin Othman Al-Homsi told us, he said: Abu Haywa told us, he said: Shuaib told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Al-Munkadir, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, in a similar way: When the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, “when he bowed, he would say: O God, for You I kneel, and in You I believe.” “And to You I have submitted, and in You I have put my trust. You are my Lord. My hearing, my sight, my blood, my flesh, my bones, and my nerves are humbled to God, Lord of the Worlds.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"634","636 Yahya bin Uthman told us, he said: Ibn Himyar told us, he said: Shuaib told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Al-Munkadir, and another mentioned Before him, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman al-Araj, on the authority of Muhammad ibn Maslamah, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, “when he stood, he would pray voluntarily.” When he bows, he says: O God, to You I kneel, and in You I believe, and to You I submit, and in You I trust, You are my Lord, all my hearing and sight are humbled, And my flesh, my blood, my brain, and my sinews belong to God, Lord of the worlds.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"635","637 Qutaibah bin Saeed informed us, saying: Bakr bin Mudar told us, on the authority of Ibn Ajlan, on the authority of Ali bin Yahya al-Zarqi, on the authority of his father, On the authority of his uncle, who was Badri, he said: We were with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, when a man entered the mosque and prayed, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, entered the mosque and prayed. He looked at him without realizing it, then he left, and he came to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and returned his greetings to him, then said: “Come back and pray.” Then you did not pray.” He said: I do not know. He said in the second or in the third. He said: By the One who sent down to you the Book, I have striven, so teach me and show me. He said: : “If you want to pray, perform ablution, perform the ablution well, then stand up and face the Qiblah, then say “Allahu Akbar,” then recite, then bow until Be at ease while kneeling, then rise until you are upright standing, then prostrate until you are at ease prostrating, then raise your head until you are at ease while sitting, then Prostrate until you are confident in your prostration. If you do that, you have fulfilled your prayer, and whatever you detract from that, you are only detracting from your prayer.”"
"636","638 Muhammad bin Abdul-Ala told us, on the authority of Khaled, he said: Shu’bah told us, on the authority of Qatada, he said: I heard Anas speaking, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. May God bless him and grant him peace. He said: “Complete your bowing and prostration when you have bowed and prostrated.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"637","639 Suwayd bin Nasr told us, he said: Anba Abdullah, on the authority of Qays bin Sulaym al-Anbari, he said: Alqamah bin Wael told me, he said: he told me My father, he said: I prayed behind the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and I saw him raise his hands when he began the prayer, and when he bowed, and when he said: I heard “Allah belongs to those who praise Him.” Thus, Qais pointed towards the ears."
"638","Ismail bin Masoud told us, he said: Yazid told us, he is Ibn Zuray’, he said: Sa’id told us, on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Nasr bin Asim. He told them, on the authority of Malik bin Al-Huwaith, that he saw the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, “raising his hands when he bowed, and when he raised his head from bowing, until he aligns them with the branches of his ears.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"639","Amr bin Ali told us, he said: Yahya bin Saeed told us, he said: Malik bin Anas told us, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Salim, on the authority of his father The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace: “When he entered prayer, he would raise his hands at the level of his shoulders, and when he raised his head from bowing, he would do something like That is, and when he said: God hears those who praise Him, he said: “Our Lord, praise be to You,” and he did not raise his hands between the two prostrations.”"
"640","642 Mahmoud bin Ghaylan Al-Maruzi told us, he said: Abba Waki’, he said: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Asim bin Kulayb, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin Al-Aswad, on the authority of Alqamah, on the authority of Abdullah, that he said: Shall I not lead with you the prayer of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace? “So he prayed and did not raise his hands except once.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"641","Suwayd bin Nasr told us, he said: Abba Abdullah, on the authority of Malik bin Anas, on the authority of Ibn Shihab, on the authority of Salem, on the authority of Ibn Umar, that the Messenger God, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to say: “When he opened the prayer, he would raise his hands to the level of his shoulders, and when he said “Allahu Akbar” for bowing, and when he raised his head from bowing He raised them in the same way as well, and said: “God hears whoever praises Him. Our Lord, praise be to You,” and he did not do that when prostrating."
"642","644 Ishaq bin Ibrahim told us, he said: Abba Abd al-Razzaq, he said: Abba Muammar, on the authority of al-Zuhri, on the authority of Abu Salamah, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, He said: Whenever the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, raised his head from the rak’ah, he would say: “O God, our Lord, to You be praise.”"
"643","645 Hanad bin Al-Sari informed us, on the authority of Ibn Uyaynah, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Anas, that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, fell from a horse on He split his right side, so they went in to visit him, and the time for prayer came. When he finished the prayer, he said: “The imam is only to be followed in prayer, so when he bows, bow down. And when He raises, raise them, and when He says: God hears those who praise Him, then say: Our Lord, and to You be praise.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"644","646 Muhammad bin Salamah Abu Al-Harith Al-Masry told us, he said: Anba Ibn Al-Qasim, on the authority of Malik, he said: Nu’aym bin Abdullah told me, On the authority of Ali bin Yahya Al-Zarqi, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Rifa’ah bin Rafi’, he said: “One day we were praying behind the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. When he raised his head from the rak’ah, he said: “God hears those who praise Him.” Then a man behind him said: Our Lord, and to You is praise, abundant and good and blessed. When the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, left, he said: “Who was the one speaking above?” A man said: “I am, O Messenger of God.” The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “I saw thirty-four kings hastening to see which of them Should he write it first? \ (Peace Be Upon Him)"""""
"645","647 Qutayba bin Saeed informed us, on the authority of Malik, on the authority of Sumayy, on the authority of Abu Salih, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, And he said: “If the imam says: God hears those who praise Him, then say: Our Lord, and to You be praise, for he is the one whose words agree with the words of the angels.” He will be forgiven for his previous sins.”"
"646","648 Ismail bin Masoud told us, he said: Khaled told us, he said: Saeed told us, on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Yunus bin Jubayr, on the authority of Hattan. Bin Abdullah, that he testified that Abu Musa said: The Prophet of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, addressed us, explained to us our Sunnah, and taught us our prayers. He said: “When you pray, straighten your rows, then let one of you lead in prayer. When the imam says “Allahu Akbar,” say “Allahu Akbar,” and if he recites “Allahu Akbar,” then “Allahu Akbar.” And when he recites “Allahu Akbar.” On them, nor those who go astray, so say: Amen, God will answer you, so when he says the greatest and bows, then say the greatest and bow, for the imam bows before you and rises before you.” The Prophet of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “So do that, and when he says: God hears those who praise Him, then say: O God, our Lord, praise be to You.” God listens to you, for God said through His Prophet: God hears whoever praises Him, so when he says “Allahu Akbar” and prostrates, “Allahu Akbar” and prostrate, for the Imam He prostrates before you and raises himself before you.” The Prophet of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “So it is like that. If it is at the time of sitting, then let it be.” From the first thing one of you says: Good greetings and prayers are for God. Peace be upon you, O Prophet, and God’s mercy and blessings be upon us. Peace be upon us and upon our servants. God is the righteous, I bear witness that there is no god but God, and that Muhammad is His servant and Messenger, seven words, which are the greeting of prayer.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"647","649 Ya’qub bin Ibrahim told us, he said: Ibn Ulayya told us, he said: Shu’bah reported, on the authority of Al-Hakam, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin Abi Layla, on the authority of Al-Baraa bin Aazib, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, “used to bow and when he raised his head from bowing and prostration, and what between the two prostrations, close to the same.”"
"648","650 Abu Dawud Sulayman bin Saif Al-Harrani told us, he said: Saeed bin Amir told us, he said: Hisham bin Hassan told us, on the authority of Qais Ibn Saad, on the authority of Ata’, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace: “When he said: God hears those who praise Him, he would say: Oh God Our Lord, praise be to You, filling the heavens and the earth, and filling whatever you wish after that.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"649","651 Muhammad bin Ismail bin Ibrahim told us, he said: Yahya told us, he said: Ibrahim, who is Ibn Nafi’, told us, on the authority of Wahb Ibn Minas al-Adani, on the authority of Sa`id ibn Jubayr, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, “when he wanted to prostrate after the rak’ah He says: O God, praise be to You, filling the heavens and filling the earth, and filling whatever You wish after that. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"650","652 Amr ibn Hisham al-Harrani Abu Umayyah informed us, saying: Mukhlid told us, on the authority of Sa`id ibn Abd al-Aziz, on the authority of Atiya ibn Qais, on the authority of Qaza bin Yahya, on the authority of Abu Sa`id al-Khudri, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, “used to say when he said: God hears those who Praise be to Him, our Lord. To You is praise, filling the heavens, filling the earth, and filling whatever you wish afterward, worthy of praise and glory, the truth of what the servant said, We are all your servants, we will not dispute what you have given, and your diligence will not benefit you.”"
"651","653 Humayd ibn Masada al-Basri informed us, saying: Yazid ibn Zuray` narrated to us, saying: Shu`bah narrated to us, on the authority of Amr ibn Murrah, on the authority of Abi Hamza, on the authority of a man from Banu Abs, on the authority of Hudhayfah, that he prayed with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, one night, and he heard “when he grew up He said: God is the Greatest, the Possessor of power, kingdom, pride, and greatness, and he used to say while bowing: Glory be to my Lord the Great, and behold He raised his head from bowing, and said: To my Lord, praise be to my Lord, and in his prostration: Glory be to my Lord, the Most High, and between the two prostrations: My Lord, forgive me, my Lord Forgive me, and his standing and bowing, and when he raised his head from bowing and prostration, and what was between the two prostrations, were close to the same.”"
"652","Ishaq bin Ibrahim told us, he said: Abba Jarir, on the authority of Sulaiman al-Taymi, on the authority of Abu Majliz, on the authority of Anas bin Malik, he said: “The Messenger of Allah Qunut God, may God bless him and grant him peace, for a month after bowing, supplicating against arrogant, disobedient, and disobedient people who have disobeyed God and His Messenger.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"653","Qutaibah bin Saeed told us, he said: Hammad told us, on the authority of Ayyub, on the authority of Ibn Sirin, on the authority of Anas bin Malik, he was asked, “Did the Messenger of Allah recite Qunoot?” He, may God bless him and grant him peace, in the morning prayer. He said: Yes. Then he was asked: Before or after bowing? He said: After bowing? (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"654","656 Ismail bin Masoud told us, he said: Bishr bin al-Mufaddal told us, on the authority of Yunus, on the authority of Ibn Sirin, he said: Some of those who prayed told me With the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, the morning prayer. “When he said: God has heard those who praised Him in the second rak’ah, he stood up for a while.”"
"655","657 Muhammad bin Mansour told us, he said: Sufyan told us, he said: We preserved from Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Saeed, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: “When The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, raised his head from the second rak’ah of the morning prayer and said: O God, save Al-Walid bin Al-Walid and Salamah bin Hisham. And Ayyash bin Abi Rabi’ah, in Mecca. Oh God, intensify your influence on Mudar, and grant them years like the years of Joseph.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"656","658 Amr bin Uthman told us, he said: Baqiyya told us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Hamza, he said: Muhammad told me, he said: Sa’id bin told me Al-Musayyab, and Abu Salama bin Abdul-Rahman, that Abu Hurairah used to narrate, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to make supplication during prayer. When he says: God hears whoever praises Him, our Lord, and to You be praise. Then he says while standing before he prostrates: O God, save Al-Walid bin Al-Walid. And Salama bin Hisham, and Ayyash bin Abi Rabi’ah, are among the believers. Oh God, intensify your influence on Mudar, and make it upon them like the teeth of Joseph. Then he would say: God is Great, and the people of the suburb of Mudar would prostrate on that day, opposing the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"657","659 Suleiman bin Salam Abu Dawud Al-Balkhi told us, he said: Al-Nadr told us, he said: Abba Hisham, on the authority of Yahya, on the authority of Abu Salamah, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: “I will bring nearer to you the prayer of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace.” He said: Abu Hurairah used to say Qunoot in the last rak’ah of The noon prayer, the last evening prayer, and the morning prayer, after he says: God hears those who praise Him, so he prays for the believers and curses the disbelievers.”"
"658","660 Ubayd Allah bin Saeed told us, on the authority of Abdul Rahman, he said: Sufyan and Shu’bah told us, on the authority of Amr bin Murrah, and he said: Amr bin Ali, who said: Yahya told us, on the authority of Shu’bah, and Sufyan, who said: Amr bin Murrah told us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Laila, on the authority of Al-Baraa bin Aazib, “The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to perform Qunoot in the morning and evening prayers.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"659","661 Muhammad bin Al-Muthanna told us, he said: Abu Dawud told us, he said: Shu’bah told us, on the authority of Qatada, and Hisham told us, on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Anas, that the Prophet, the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, observed Qunoot for a month. Shu’bah said: “He cursed men,” and Hisham said: “He calls upon “Among the Arabs,” then he left him after bowing. This is the saying of Hisham, and Shu’bah said, on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Anas, that The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said, “For a month, he cursed Ra’la, Dhakwan, and Lahyan.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"660","662 Ishaq bin Ibrahim told us, he said: Anba Abd al-Razzaq, Muammar told us, on the authority of al-Zuhri, on the authority of Salim, on the authority of his father, that he heard The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, when he raised his head in the morning prayer of the last rak’ah, said: “O God, curse so-and-so and so-and-so, who prayed against people from Hypocrites, so God revealed, ‘You have nothing to do with the matter, or turn to them or punish them, for they are wrongdoers.’” Abu Abd al-Rahman said: No. This hadith was narrated by none of the trustworthy people except Mu’ammar."
